  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "progress.piece_map",
      "help": "Where a download's data has arrived, in status, wait, and the TUI's watch stream: 64 characters, one per equal run of the torrent's pieces in order. 0 to 8 are eighths of the run's selected pieces that passed their hash check, and - is a run with no selected piece. Absent before the engine first samples it, which needs the file list, and once the download is done"
    },
    {
      "name": "result.releases[].quality",
      "help": "What the release name says about the picture: resolution is 2160p, 1080p, 720p, or sd, codec is h264, hevc, or av1, and each is null when the name does not say. hdr is true for an HDR10, HDR10+, or Dolby Vision tag"
    },
    {
      "name": "result.query.profile",
      "help": "What the results were ranked for. screen and playback each carry a value and a source, detected or override, and are null when nothing is known. max_size comes from the preferences that torrential setup saves. room, arch, and language are detected, and room is the bytes a download may take in the download folder. detected is null until the engine finishes detecting the machine after it starts. Within equal relevance, results that fit max_size, the room, and the player come first, then official and lawful sources, then the resolution closest to the screen, then the machine's CPU architecture, then releases in the system language"
    }
  ],
  "next": null
